{title:BNR annual report Step 1: Build the candidate}

{title:What this step does}

{pstd}
Step 1 builds the private annual-report candidate, its public-health update,
website page and metadata from the selected approved public releases and the
reviewed year-specific content.

{title:Before you run it}

{pstd}
Confirm that the event and mortality releases are approved and published. The
year-specific interpretation, special chapter and contents files must be
complete and reviewed.

{title:What to enter}

{phang}{bf:Report year and version} identify the annual report candidate.

{phang}{bf:CVD-event release} and {bf:mortality release} identify the approved
public datasets used to build the report.

{phang}{bf:Authorise replacement} should normally remain unticked. Rebuilding
a candidate invalidates any earlier review or approval of that candidate.

{title:After running}

{pstd}
Review the complete candidate package, including both PDFs, the website page
and metadata. When the candidate and disclosure review are satisfactory,
continue to annual report Step 2.

{title:Full instructions}

{pstd}
See the {browse "https://uwi-bnr.github.io/info-hub/technical/workflows/reporting/annual-report.html":Technical Manual: Build, approve and publish an annual CVD report}.
